# low-observable — Cursor AI project rules

You are assisting on a Unity game whose simulation core is engine-free C# (EKF, particle filter,
data association, Seeker AI). Same conventions as turtlebot-rfid-slam.

## Authoritative sources (read in order)

1. `AGENTS.md` — repo map, hard rules, quality gates.
2. `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — scoped rules by path.
3. `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/estimation-primer.md` before touching `core/`.

## Hard constraints

- `core/Runtime/` never references UnityEngine and stays at C# 9.
- Rendering and the autopilot read beliefs, never ground truth (except the reveal screen and F1 overlay).
- All randomness through `Maths.Rng` streams derived from the episode seed.
- Game-feel numbers live in `TuningParameters` and are documented in `docs/tuning.md`.

## Quality gates

- `make lint`, `make test`; `make sim` when a change affects balance.

## Output style

- Use code citations (`startLine:endLine:path`) when showing existing code.
- Prefer focused diffs; avoid unrelated refactors.
